n</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1827</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-smidt">Johann Smidt</a> founds <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremerhaven">Bremerhaven</a> at the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weser">Weser</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1857</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norddeutscher-lloyd">Norddeutscher Lloyd</a> is founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremen">Bremen</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1947</span><span class="rf-text">The Land of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremen">Bremen</a> is re-established with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremerhaven">Bremerhaven</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1949</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremen">Bremen</a> becomes a state of the Federal Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a></span></li></ol>
